Windows server and installer app code unchanged. Main remains frozen.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Layer 2 Independent Silero VAD Hotfix, 2026-10-24.
Windows Inno Setup version 0.4.6. Installs and verifies the official offline
Silero VAD 6.2.3 TorchScript model; displays separate candidate speech intervals,
without asserting target-speaker identity or changing learning approvals.
Adds a localized clipping warning for long recordings with short saturated
passages. Android source and Main unchanged. Real model and full-regression
validation are mandatory gates in the Windows installer build.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Windows build dependency recovery, 2026-10-24.
The full regression runner now uses the exact .installer_venv Python and
verifies requests immediately before collecting tests. If requests cannot be
imported, it repairs that isolated environment and rechecks, failing the
installer build safely if still unavailable. Windows Inno version stays
0.4.6, Silero Layer 2 unchanged, Android unchanged, Main frozen.

Branch 2 Phase 3 full Windows dependency-identity follow-up, 2026-10-24.
Windows Inno Setup version still 0.4.6; no Android or model changes.
All application pip installs, test execution, offline model checks and
PyInstaller now use the same explicit .installer_venv Python. Before pytest,
the builder verifies and repairs requests 2.32.3 and NLTK 3.9.1 if missing,
and runs pip check against that interpreter. Windows build verification
is still required; the prior 237-pass test was before this source update.

Branch 2 Phase 3 full runtime dependency preflight, 2026-10-25.
Inno Setup version stays 0.4.6; Android and all 13 analysis layers unchanged.
Windows installer now checks every pinned direct speech/audio/build package
inside the isolated venv, repairs missing soundfile/sounddevice/Silero and
other known packages, verifies installed versions, runs pip check, full
regressions, then real Silero inference before packaging. Main stays frozen.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Parent PC frozen-server startup hotfix, 2026-10-25.
Inno version remains 0.4.6; no changes to Android, recording files, Silero,
or the 13 speech-analysis layers. The local HTTP server explicitly disables
unused WebSocket protocols, pins Uvicorn's HTTP protocol to h11 and bundles it.
The existing frozen --self-test now executes actual Uvicorn protocol loading
so the missing websockets.legacy startup regression stops the build.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Background / Phoneme Integrity Hotfix, 2026-10-25.
Inno version remains 0.4.6 and Android is unchanged. Digits in word-ASR
hypotheses are normalized for review-only phoneme agreement (unsupported
numbers explicitly remain unresolved); borderline stretched ASR word spans
raise review warnings. Ranked word suggestions outside independent Silero
candidate activity are retained as unverified suggestions instead of ordinary
word candidates. No audio, CTC observation, approval or learning is changed.
New review-only within-utterance prosody excludes long session pauses and
disclaims speaker identification. Main remains frozen. See
PHASE3_BACKGROUND_PHONEME_INTEGRITY_HOTFIX_20261025.md for validation.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Word-ASR / Silero and Activity-Window Quality Hotfix,
2026-10-25. Inno Setup version remains 0.4.6; Android is unchanged. Adds
review-only word-ASR segment timing crosschecks against independent Silero
activity intervals, separate window-based amplitude diagnostics to explain
whole-session intentional-pause bias, and a caregiver-facing summary of
independent recognition disagreements. No modification of original WAVs,
protected acoustic observations, candidate transcripts, approvals, or learning.
See PHASE3_SPEECH_CROSSCHECK_QUALITY_HOTFIX_20261025.md for test results.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Retroactive Recording Titles and Search Hotfix, 2026-10-25.
Inno version stays 0.4.6 and Android remains unchanged. Parent PC Recording
History displays deterministic suggested titles for existing WAVs using saved
metadata and verified analysis only. User-defined recording titles, searchable
tags/notes, bulk Save Suggested Titles and revert-to-suggestion controls are
stored in a separate audited, atomic local index. Existing SILERO/word/phoneme
cross-checks, baseline 13 layers, audio/observation/learning evidence and Main
remain untouched. See PHASE3_RECORDING_TITLE_TAG_SEARCH_HOTFIX_20261025.md.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Recording History Search / Sort Controls Repair, 2026-10-25.
Windows Inno Setup version advanced to 0.4.7 so the newly installed repair
can be distinguished from earlier 0.4.6 builds. Adds visible Search and
Apply Sort buttons, Enter-to-search, clickable column headings with reverse
sorting, all 14 sort directions, a results/status message and build marker.
Newest/oldest sorting uses saved recording creation times, not WAV file mtime.
Previously saved, identity-verified Parent PC ASR word suggestions are included
in Recording History searches without approving them or learning from them.
All earlier integrated hotfixes are carried forward; Main and Android are
unchanged. See PHASE3_RECORDING_HISTORY_SEARCH_SORT_REPAIR_20261025.md.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Windows Regression Test Path Compatibility Repair, 2026-10-25.
Fixes two installer-blocking assertions introduced by the Recording History
Search / Sort hotfix. Test fixtures use pathlib.Path; the assertions previously
expected literal POSIX-style '/fake/name.wav' strings, which fail on Windows
where Path displays '\\fake\\name.wav'. Expected table identifiers now use
native Path formatting as well. No application behavior, recording data,
analysis, learning, Android code, or installer prerequisites changed.
Inno version remains 0.4.7 because the installed application is identical.
See PHASE3_WINDOWS_RECORDING_SORT_TEST_COMPATIBILITY_20261025.md.

Branch 2 Phase 3 Android Caregiver Child Name on Upload, 2026-10-25.
Android version 3.3.3/code9; matching Windows Parent PC installer 0.4.8.
The phone asks the caregiver for an optional child name before Send & Analyze.
It can use the already saved Student Profile name by explicit caregiver choice.
The label is saved as immutable per-recording events outside the original WAV
and identity metadata, sent to both receipt and analysis endpoints, echoed by
the new Parent PC to prevent silent loss, and indexed/displayed as a searchable
"(phone label)" in Parent PC Recording History. No automatic mapping of a
shared phone speaker ID to a child, no changes to observation evidence or
learning approval, no retroactive renaming of previously uploaded WAVs. The
existing 13-layer analysis and Main remain unchanged. See
PHASE3_ANDROID_CHILD_NAME_UPLOAD_HOTFIX_20261025.md.

